# Smart Pesticide Residue Detection System

A low-cost, portable fruit screening prototype that combines multi-sensor data and TinyML on the STM32F407VET6 microcontroller.

> This is a screening tool, not a replacement for laboratory testing. Comparison with lab analysis is future work.

## Project Overview
The system reads colour, pH, gas, temperature and humidity from a fruit sample, and a camera image. Two small TinyML models run on the STM32 board. The result is shown on an OLED display, and a buzzer alerts for unsafe readings.

## Hardware Components
- STM32F407VET6 microcontroller
- 0.96" OLED display
- DHT11 temperature and humidity sensor
- TCS34725 colour sensor
- pH probe
- MQ135 gas sensor
- OV2640 camera
- Buzzer
- Light box (white sunboard) with LED lighting

## Software Tools
- STM32CubeIDE
- TinyML (models running on the STM32)

## Features
- Multi-sensor fusion: colour, pH, gas, temperature, humidity and camera
- On-device TinyML, no cloud needed
- OLED result pages and buzzer alert
- MQ135 freshness status: FRESH (below 1.5), RIPENING (1.5 to 3.0), SPOILED (3.0 or more)
- Low cost (about Rs. 11,500)

